# Development-only router, selected by conf/localhost.conf.
#
# The production router (conf/routes) deliberately does NOT mount the phon
# emulator: phon is a teaching and manual-testing tool, its Guice bindings live
# in PhonModule, and PhonModule is enabled only in conf/localhost.conf. Keeping
# it out of the production router means there is no route, no controller and no
# binding to expose - rather than a route that something has to remember to
# block.

# Order matters: conf/routes ends in a catch-all that hands any unmatched path to
# MarkdownController, so mounting it first would swallow /phonyPhone before the phon
# router is ever consulted.
->      /phonyPhone                      phon.Routes
->      /                                router.Routes
